<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>CSS Display & Position Tasks</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background-color: #f4f4f4;
      color: #000000;
      min-height: 2000px; /* Ensure page is scrollable for fixed/sticky demo */
    }

    h1, h2, h3 {
      text-align: center;
      color: #a600ff;
      margin-top: 40px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
      padding-bottom: 10px;
    }

    section {
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 20px;
      background-color: white;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .box {
      background-color: #3498db;
      color: white;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 5px;
      border: 1px solid #2980b9;
      text-align: center;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    /* Task 1 — Display Basics */
    .display-block-container .box {
      /* display: block is default for div, but explicitly set for clarity */
      display: block; 
      background-color: #2ecc71;
    }
    .display-inline-container .box {
      display: inline; /* Items flow like text, width/height ignored */
      background-color: #e74c3c;
    }
    .display-inline-block-container .box {
      display: inline-block; /* Items flow like text, but respect width/height */
      width: 100px;
      height: 50px;
      line-height: 50px; /* Center text vertically */
      background-color: #f39c12;
    }

    /* Task 2 — Hidden Element */
    .hidden-paragraph {
      display: none; /* Element is completely removed from the document flow */
      background-color: #9b59b6;
      color: white;
      padding: 10px;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    /* Task 3 — Position Basics */
    .position-container {
      position: relative; /* Crucial for absolute children to position relative to this container */
      height: 250px;
      border: 2px dashed #ffa200;
      background-color: #ecf0f1;
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding: 10px;
    }
    .static-box {
      position: static; /* Default position, element flows normally */
      background-color: #1abc9c;
      width: 100px;
      height: 50px;
    }
    .relative-box {
      position: relative; /* Positioned relative to its normal position */
      top: 20px;
      left: 20px;
      background-color: #8e44ad;
      width: 100px;
      height: 50px;
    }
    .absolute-box {
      position: absolute; /* Positioned relative to its nearest positioned ancestor */
      bottom: 10px;
      right: 10px;
      background-color: #d35400;
      width: 100px;
      height: 50px;
    }

    /* Task 4 — Fixed & Sticky */
    .fixed-box {
      position: fixed; /* Positioned relative to the viewport, stays put on scroll */
      top: 20px;
      right: 20px;
      background-color: #c0392b;
      color: white;
      padding: 10px 15px;
      border-radius: 5px;
      z-index: 1000; /* Ensure it stays on top */
    }
    .sticky-header {
      position: sticky; /* Sticks to the top when scrolled past its normal position */
      top: 0;
      background-color: #ff9500;
      color: white;
      padding: 15px;
      text-align: center;
      z-index: 999; /* Below fixed box */
      box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
    }

    /* Task 5 — Mini Project: Menu Toggle */
    .menu-button {
      display: block;
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 10px 20px;
      font-size: 1.1em;
      cursor: pointer;
      background-color: #2980b9;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 5px;
    }
    .menu {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      background-color: #ecf0f1;
      border: 1px solid #bdc3c7;
      border-radius: 5px;
      max-width: 300px;
      text-align: left;
      /* Initially hidden */
      display: none; 
    }
    .menu li {
      padding: 8px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px dashed #ccc;
    }
    .menu li:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }
    .menu a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #34495e;
      display: block;
    }
    .menu a:hover {
      color: #2980b9;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

  </style>
</head>
<body>
<button class="fixed-box" onclick="location.href='about.html'">click here</button>
  <header class="sticky-header">
    <h1>Website Header</h1>
  </header>

  <h1>CSS Display & Position Properties</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Task 1 — Display Basics</h2>

    <h3>`display: block`</h3>
    <p>Block-level elements take up the full width available and start on a new line.</p>
    <div class="display-block-container">
      <div class="box">Block 1</div>
      <div class="box">Block 2</div>
      <div class="box">Block 3</div>
    </div>

    <h3>`display: inline`</h3>
    <p>Inline elements only take up as much width as necessary and do not start on a new line. Width and height properties are ignored.</p>
    <div class="display-inline-container">
      <div class="box">Inline 1</div>
      <div class="box">Inline 2</div>
      <div class="box">Inline 3</div>
    </div>

    <h3>`display: inline-block`</h3>
    <p>Inline-block elements flow like inline elements but respect width and height properties.</p>
    <div class="display-inline-block-container">
      <div class="box">Inline-Block 1</div>
      <div class="box">Inline-Block 2</div>
      <div class="box">Inline-Block 3</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
 <h2>Hidden Element Task</h2>
  <p>This paragraph is visible to everyone.</p>
  <p class="hidden-text">You can’t see this text because display is set to none.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Task 3 — Position Basics</h2>
    <p>Demonstrates `static`, `relative`, and `absolute` positioning within a `relative` container.</p>
    <div class="position-container">
      <div class="box static-box">Static</div>
      <div class="box relative-box">Relative (shifted)</div>
      <div class="box absolute-box">Absolute (bottom-right)</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Task 4 — Fixed & Sticky (Scroll to see effect)</h2>
    <p>The "Fixed Box" in the top-right corner stays in place as you scroll.</p>
    <p>The "Sticky Header" above this section will stick to the top of the viewport once you scroll past it.</p>
